# A bow-only bandit from BanditCreator shoots at a moving player. It runs the game's bow combat tree (CombatTreeModule):
# the default combat tree has no bow branch, and its melee fallback only shoots point blank at a target standing still.
# Once the player moves away, a bandit on the fallback only loads its quiver while it follows. Debug build only.
#
# dotnet run --project tools/Drova.TestRunner -c Debug -- tests/scenarios/bow_bandit.scn

default hero 5
default slot 0

launch A
A wait ready=1 timeout=240
A wait saves=separate timeout=60
A load $hero $slot
A wait world=1 timeout=240

A invincible on
A bandit Bow 300 0
# The body keeps the template's name. Nothing else built from the template stands near this save's spawn.
A expect actlog start Template_Human_NPC contains logging timeout=30
A expect actlog read contains "PrimaryAttack.0:AA_Bow_HuntingBow_Attack_00[AHSKLR" timeout=30

# The player walks away: full draws released at the moving target, and no quiver reload.
A walk -1 0 15
A actlog start Template_Human_NPC
A expect actlog read contains "PrimaryAttack.0:AA_Bow_HuntingBow_Attack_00[AHSKLR" timeout=12
A expect actlog read !contains "Quiver"

# The arrows land, at the latest once the walk is over: a moving player can sidestep them.
A invincible off
A expect health me !contains "40/40" timeout=30
